      <description align="left" color="orange" colored="true" height="410" resized="false" width="713" x="10" y="156">You may find the demo video &lt;a href="https://academy.rapidminer.com/learn/video/aggregations-demo"&gt;here!&lt;br&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Aggregate the Transaction Data, to get ave &amp;amp; sum of TransactionValue, and max Date for each CustomerId&lt;br&gt;2. Pivot a copy of the original Transaction Data to get count of payment method for each customer and PaymentMethod with one row per CustomerId and one column per PaymentMethod&lt;br&gt;5. Join the pivoted copy and aggregated copy with an inner join on CustomerId&lt;br&gt;(Optional) Consider replace Missing with zero&lt;br&gt;(Optional) Consider Loading Data, the auxillary data: Hotel App Joins data&lt;br&gt;--- Then with the original data selected, merge the new data in with an inner join on CustomerId&lt;br&gt;Add to Process&lt;br&gt;(Optional) Rename average(TransactionValue) to AverageTransactionValue, maximum(Date) to MostRecentTransactionDate, sum(TransactionValue) to TotalTransactionValue, and Geschlect to Gender&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;-- Optional - Use Turbo Prep instead--&lt;br&gt;1. Run the existing process and then in results, Open in Turbo Prep.&lt;br&gt;2. Get another copy of the Transaction Data from the repository&lt;br&gt;3. Pivot the original Transaction Data, to get ave &amp;amp; sum of TransactionValue for each CustomerId&lt;br&gt;4. Pivot the copy to get count of payment method for each customer and PaymentMethod with one row per CustomerId and one column per PaymentMethod&lt;br&gt;5. Select Original data from process, Merge the copy with an inner join on CustomerId&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
    </process>
